timate daughter her  assassination attempt is a culmination  of 20 years of pain knowing that he  abandoned her mother although batman  stops her from actually murdering  falcone the riddler finishes the grim  job with a rifle  thankfully because of riddler left  himself vulnerable by staying near the  crime scene it doesn't take long for the  gcpd to track him down and haul edward  nashton over to the arkham correctional  facility  yes it's time for the typical villain  explains their plan in great detail part  of the movie nashton's explanation  actually serves a key purpose this time  beyond lazy exposition he reveals a true  extent of the corruption that has  gripped gotham for decades and forces  the audience to face in an easy  comparison between himself and the caped  crusader you see ridler used to work for  the wayne's renewal project as a  forensic accountant and that's where he  discovered the dark truth while the  wealthy elite got richer by skimming  from renewal nashton was growing up in  one of the orphanages that should have  benefited from that money enduring a  horrific childhood in squalor he then  makes a disturbing confession he was  only spurred into action when he saw how  batman was tackling crime on gotham  streets yes bruce helped bring the  riddler to life he inspired the killer  to take the leap into vigilantism  meaning there's plenty of blood on those  bad hands of his to be fair the film  makes a point of showing just how brutal  batman is to the point that the  civilians aren't even sure if he's a  friend or foe it's hardly surprising  that other self-righteous foe could  follow in his footsteps unfortunately  there's little time for soul searching  here since riddler has already rigged  bombs around gotham seawall as a final  act in his war on the city  the final stage of the riddler's plan  sees the villain bomb the sea wall which  floods most of the city in a moment  comic readers will recognize from the  pages of the new 52's zero year event  the riddler's entire game has been about  forcing the corrupt into the light and  unearthing their crimes as well as  cleansing the city of its collective  sins by flooding the entire city he  plans to purge gotham of the ruts that  has taken hold while forcing the  citizens to start afresh although the  villain succeeds in flooding the city he  has another surprise up his sleeve as a  horde of his faithful followers are  waiting in the gotham arena which has  been set up as the emergency shelter for  survivors thankfully batman and catwoman  show up to dish out a beating this is  the first time batman truly feels like a  hero in the film rather than just a  brawler feeding his own thirst for  vengeance it's a critical moment that  draws a clear contrast between batman's  brand of vigilantism and riddlers after  all one vigilante is trying to  indiscriminately kill thousands of  people while the other is trying to  protect them even when he's at the point  of exhaustion on the floor batman uses a  suspicious green adrenaline shot to  force himself up so he can stop one of  the shooters from killing selena  ultimately this dynamic duo manages to  save the day as for that suspicious  green liquid we've gotta guess  it's the venom  yes riddler has been defeated but only  to a point it saves a lot that the  losing villains still manage to flood an  entire city while also single-handedly  proving that institutional corruption is  rife within the mayor's office and the  gcpd but since riddler is pretty  deranged here it's no surprise that he's  locked up in arkham and this is a comic  book movie after all so it's time for  that all-important sequel bait back in  2020 rumors swelled that director and  co-writer matt reeves was planning to  include the joker in his batman trilogy  and it seems this early speculation was  spot on while the riddler is crying in a  cell an eerie voice starts to creep in  from the cell next to his this menacing  neighbor has a scary smile as he tells  the riddler that everyone loves an  encore before saying you know what they  say one day you're on top of the world  and the next day you're a clown clown  joker you get it it's a brief scene but  eternal star barry kyogin really does a  lot with her it's unsurprising since he  already proved he can tackle difficult  characters thanks to his work in  american animals and the killing of a  sacred deer a joker riddler alliance  would be fun but it would be much more  interesting if gotham got caught between  the two we could be headed for a story  inspired by the war of jokes and riddles  so where does this all leave batman by  the time the action in gotham arena is  over he's immediately on disaster aid  duty he starts a film with a devil may  care attitude but he slowly realizes  that he can be a positive force for  changing gotham by trying to help its  people not just as muscle against  muggers and serial killers the prime  example of this is the way he leads some  of the survivors out of the wreckage it  absolutely hammers home the film's  central moral quandary what makes batman  good and riddler evil the answer appears  to be that for batman there's an honest  moral calculation between means and ends  it's clear to the hero that he can do  more when he helps a young girl who's  been evacuated she grabs his hand out of  fear and he's there to silently reassure  her that everything is going to be okay  despite his earlier claim  i'm vengeance  he's more than the retributive hand of  justice he also helps the people who  have been harmed riddler has no interest  in helping and for him the punishment  appears to be an end in and of itself  considering the film starts with batman  brutalizing a gang of thugs in the rain  this is all quite the optimistic and  hopeful development  he's not the only one who's changing  their outlook on life selena is also  ready to change her situation by the  time the credits roll  miss kyle decides to leave gotham for  bloodhaven a reference to the city  nightwing usually makes his home in the  hope that she can make a new life there  it's unsurprising that she needs a fresh  start after enduring so much trauma  thanks to her mobster father  unfortunately she can't persuade bruce  to join her because he's got a renewed  sense of faith when it comes to his  crusade to save gotham from itself but  she'll probably be back for the sequel  it'll be interesting to see whether  selena discovers his billionaire alter  ego in the future and whether that makes  him seem more or less eligible as a  romantic partner maybe we're not so  different  who are you under there  so the bat and cats say their goodbyes  in a race through gotham sprawling  necropolis by the angsty emo kids that  they are they even speed off in separate  directions with bruce heading back into  the city toward the light of the bat  signal check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about the batman are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

